the research question.\",\"search_leads\":[\"subgroup stratified clinical NLP model evaluation F1\"]},{\"kind\":\"mechanism\",\"requirement\":\"Specify that train, validation, and test partitions are patient-disjoint so repeated notes from one person cannot leak across partitions.\",\"must_mention\":[],\"reason\":\"A generic split does not prevent duplicated patient language or longitudinal notes from inflating validation performance.\",\"search_leads\":[\"clinical NLP patient-level split data leakage\"]},{\"kind\":\"term\",\"requirement\":\"Expand ICD and SNOMED CT at first use rather than assuming familiarity with clinical coding vocabularies.\",\"must_mention\":[\"International Classification of Diseases\",\"SNOMED Clinical Terms\"],\"reason\":\"The intended novice audience may not understand the coding systems used in disease phenotypes and structured EHR fields.\",\"search_leads\":[\"ICD SNOMED CT definitions clinical coding\"]}]}", "observable": {"verdict": "add", "additions": [{"kind": "mechanism", "requirement": "Trace one synthetic patient from raw EHR fields through extraction, CDC WONDER mapping, phenotype assignment, and prevalence numerator/denominator contribution.", "must_mention": ["CDC WONDER"], "reason": "Examples and workflow stages do not guarantee one complete record-to-result demonstration showing how the pieces connect.", "search_leads": ["clinical NLP patient record ethnicity phenotype prevalence workflow"]}, {"kind": "comparison", "requirement": "State whether the selected CDC WONDER database supplies only a label taxonomy or also supports a valid prevalence benchmark against the EHR cohort.", "must_mention": ["CDC WONDER"], "reason": "The plan could conflate borrowing subgroup labels with comparing prevalence estimates from datasets having different outcomes, populations, or denominators.", "search_leads": ["CDC WONDER database prevalence denominator mortality population"]}, {"kind": "term", "requirement": "Name a runnable beginner software